{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHotkeySequences(definitions, commonOptions?): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequences.ts#L68","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeySequences.ts:68"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React hook for registering multiple keyboard shortcut sequences at once (Vim-style)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses the singleton SequenceManager. Accepts a dynamic array of definitions so you can\nregister variable-length lists without violating the rules of hooks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callbacks and options are synced on every render to avoid stale closures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definitions with an empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sequence"},{"type":"text","value":" are skipped (no registration)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"definitions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceDefinition.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeySequenceDefinition"}]},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array of sequence definitions to register"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"commonoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"commonOptions?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeySequenceOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared options applied to all sequences (overridden by per-definition options).\nPer-row "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled: false"},{"type":"text","value":" still registers that sequence: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SequenceManager"},{"type":"text","value":" suppresses execution only (the row\nstays in the store and appears in TanStack Hotkeys devtools). Toggling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"},{"type":"text","value":" updates the existing handle\nvia "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" (no unregister/re-register churn)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function VimPalette() {\n  useHotkeySequences([\n    { sequence: ['G', 'G'], callback: () => scrollToTop() },\n    { sequence: ['D', 'D'], callback: () => deleteLine() },\n    { sequence: ['C', 'I', 'W'], callback: () => changeInnerWord(), options: { timeout: 500 } },\n  ])\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"function DynamicSequences({ items }) {\n  useHotkeySequences(\n    items.map((item) => ({\n      sequence: item.chords,\n      callback: item.action,\n      options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n    })),\n    { preventDefault: true },\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"definitions","text":"definitions","level":3},{"id":"commonoptions","text":"commonOptions?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeySequences(definitions, commonOptions?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeySequences.ts:68](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequences.ts#L68)\n\nReact hook for registering multiple keyboard shortcut sequences at once (Vim-style).\n\nUses the singleton SequenceManager. Accepts a dynamic array of definitions so you can\nregister variable-length lists without violating the rules of hooks.\n\nOptions are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options\n\nCallbacks and options are synced on every render to avoid stale closures.\n\nDefinitions with an empty `sequence` are skipped (no registration).\n\n## Parameters\n\n### definitions\n\n[`UseHotkeySequenceDefinition`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceDefinition.md)[]\n\nArray of sequence definitions to register\n\n### commonOptions?\n\n[`UseHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md) = `{}`\n\nShared options applied to all sequences (overridden by per-definition options).\n  Per-row `enabled: false` still registers that sequence: `SequenceManager` suppresses execution only (the row\n  stays in the store and appears in TanStack Hotkeys devtools). Toggling `enabled` updates the existing handle\n  via `setOptions` (no unregister/re-register churn).\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nfunction VimPalette() {\n  useHotkeySequences([\n    { sequence: ['G', 'G'], callback: () => scrollToTop() },\n    { sequence: ['D', 'D'], callback: () => deleteLine() },\n    { sequence: ['C', 'I', 'W'], callback: () => changeInnerWord(), options: { timeout: 500 } },\n  ])\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\nfunction DynamicSequences({ items }) {\n  useHotkeySequences(\n    items.map((item) => ({\n      sequence: item.chords,\n      callback: item.action,\n      options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n    })),\n    { preventDefault: true },\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHotkeySequences\ntitle: useHotkeySequences\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeySequences(definitions, commonOptions?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeySequences.ts:68](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequences.ts#L68)\n\nReact hook for registering multiple keyboard shortcut sequences at once (Vim-style).\n\nUses the singleton SequenceManager. Accepts a dynamic array of definitions so you can\nregister variable-length lists without violating the rules of hooks.\n\nOptions are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options\n\nCallbacks and options are synced on every render to avoid stale closures.\n\nDefinitions with an empty `sequence` are skipped (no registration).\n\n## Parameters\n\n### definitions\n\n[`UseHotkeySequenceDefinition`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceDefinition.md)[]\n\nArray of sequence definitions to register\n\n### commonOptions?\n\n[`UseHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md) = `{}`\n\nShared options applied to all sequences (overridden by per-definition options).\n  Per-row `enabled: false` still registers that sequence: `SequenceManager` suppresses execution only (the row\n  stays in the store and appears in TanStack Hotkeys devtools). Toggling `enabled` updates the existing handle\n  via `setOptions` (no unregister/re-register churn).\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nfunction VimPalette() {\n  useHotkeySequences([\n    { sequence: ['G', 'G'], callback: () => scrollToTop() },\n    { sequence: ['D', 'D'], callback: () => deleteLine() },\n    { sequence: ['C', 'I', 'W'], callback: () => changeInnerWord(), options: { timeout: 500 } },\n  ])\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\nfunction DynamicSequences({ items }) {\n  useHotkeySequences(\n    items.map((item) => ({\n      sequence: item.chords,\n      callback: item.action,\n      options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n    })),\n    { preventDefault: true },\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
